# Craftly Frontend — Environment Variables

## Required for all environments

```
# URL template for per-sandbox agent connections.
# Must contain the literal placeholder {sandboxId}.
# The app will show a configuration error screen if this variable is missing or invalid.
#
# Examples:
#   Local dev: http://{sandboxId}.agent.localhost:8080
#   AWS/production: https://{sandboxId}.agent.example.com
VITE_AGENT_URL_TEMPLATE=http://{sandboxId}.agent.localhost:8080
```

## Required for local development only

```
# Target for the Vite dev proxy (/api/* requests).
# Must be the local URL where your backend ingress/gateway is listening.
# No trailing slash. Do not use this in production (use a real reverse proxy instead).
#
# Example: http://127.0.0.1:8080
VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8080
```

## Notes

- **No `VITE_API_BASE_URL`** — All first-party API calls use relative paths (`/api/…`).
  The Vite dev proxy forwards them. In production, your ingress/load balancer does this.

- **No `VITE_AGENT_BASE_URL`** — Replaced by `VITE_AGENT_URL_TEMPLATE`.

- **Do not commit `.env`** — it is gitignored. Only commit `.env.example`.

- Never put real secrets, deployment URLs, or AWS hostnames in `.env.example`.
